From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:17:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09729/11362] [outer-loop] Quality scorer sweeps archived
 attempts; ops docs for REQ-ARC-WMTE-6690

arc_induction_quality.py (written this session, previously uncommitted)
now also sweeps <store>/<game>/attempts/wm_*.py and labels each row's
population (survivor vs attempt). A survivor-only degenerate rate is a
worst-attempt sample -- re-induction fires on stagnation -- so the 28%
figure this session produced was a survivor rate, not a generator rate.
With per-attempt retention the unbiased population exists on disk.

ops/status.md + ops/changelog.md: record the retention ship (append-only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
